============================================
   GROUPING SELECTOR — DEFINITION
   ============================================

   The grouping selector in CSS allows you to apply
   the same styles to multiple elements at once by
   separating them with commas.

   Why use it?
   - Reduces repeated code
   - Makes CSS cleaner and shorter
============================================
Example - 

h1, h2, p {
    color: darkblue;
    font-family: Arial;
}